	)
	(text "Notes:\n\n1. BEAPER Nano can be built in a simplified Educational Starter configuration\n   using only the components not marked as optional. One or more optional\n   analog input devices must be installed if using the analog input program\n   in Introductory Programming Activity 5.\n\n2. Headers H1-H4 can alternately be bridged with a 4-pin header socket to\n   allow a 3.3V HC-SR04P SONAR distance sensing module to be mounted \n   directly to the BEAPER Nano circuit board.\n\n3. BEAPER Nano only has 5V available when powered from screw terminal strip\n   CON1. The 5V regulator circuit (U1) and level shifter U2 are required \n   when using the motor driver (U3), or digital output headers H5-8.\n\n4. The appropriate jumper headers for JP1-JP4 must be installed to select\n   between available analog input devices. Jumpers may be hard-wired if only\n   specific analog inputs will be used."
		(at 329.692 143.256 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4bbde53d-6894-4e18-9480-84a6a26d5f6b")
	)
